def about_page():
 body=page_hero('About Solomon','Personal attention.<br>A local place to learn.','Small-group support for students across West Dublin and North Kildare, with classes based in Lucan at Scoil Áine Naofa.')+'''<section class="section"><div class="wrap two-col"><div class="content-stack" data-reveal><div class="eyebrow">Learning alongside school</div><h2>More time to<br>make it make sense.</h2><p>Solomon Grinds offers subject support that complements school learning. Its published approach centres on small groups, individual attention and preparation for exams.</p><p>Caitriona Hayes is the booking contact and is identified as the owner and a Maths teacher in her public professional profile. Her profile dates the business to 2002; we use that date instead of repeating an unverified anniversary claim.</p><p class="source-note">Sources: <a href="https://solomongrinds.ie/about-us/">Business About page ↗</a> and <a href="https://ie.linkedin.com/in/caitriona-hayes-9602426">Caitriona’s public professional profile ↗</a>.</p></div><div class="about-note"><div class="small-label">THE SOLOMON APPROACH</div><p class="display">Small groups.<br>Individual attention.<br><span class="red">A clearer next step.</span></p><div class="about-note-bottom">LUCAN · WEST DUBLIN · NORTH KILDARE</div></div></div></section><section class="section"><div class="wrap two-col"><div class="content-stack"><h2>What we can say<br>with confidence.</h2><p>The existing site describes experienced, hand-picked teaching staff, including past or present examiners. Individual teacher names and credentials are not provided there.</p><p>This concept does not add qualifications, pass rates, class-size numbers or grade promises. Ask Caitriona about the teacher and format for your chosen class.</p></div><div class="content-stack"><h3>Built around practical choices</h3><ul class="rule-list"><li><div><strong>Two teaching days</strong>Wednesday evenings and Saturdays, from the published 2026/27 timetable.</div></li><li><div><strong>Flexible attendance</strong>An advertised online platform for students who cannot attend in person. Confirm subject availability.</div></li><li><div><strong>A local base</strong>Scoil Áine Naofa on Newcastle Road, opposite SuperValu according to the business.</div></li></ul></div></div></section><section class="section"><div class="wrap"><div class="notice"><strong>Course-date correction:</strong> the existing About page still promotes Easter 2026. The dedicated course page now publishes <strong>30 March–3 April 2027</strong>. <a href="/easter-revision-leaving-junior-cert/">See the 2027 course</a>.</div></div></section>'''
 page('/about-us/','About — small-group support in Lucan','Learn about Solomon Grinds in Lucan, its small-group approach and the published hybrid learning option. Unofficial concept.',body)
